WEBVTT

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:12.200
Guy, charge from the right!
They're up higher!

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.240
Stop shouting.
I'm not your personal pilot.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.000
I'll play your little game.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.250
That's the spirit.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.920
But I've never gambled before.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:31.670
Then let's play
the simplest game in the book.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.590
Let it bloom or let it wither

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.640
The setting sun ignites the horizon

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:42.480
And the gears turn

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:55.200
When the horn blows, the flames dance

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:58.080
The story waits for no-one

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.950
Off they go, the gears are churning

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.330
A red past chases after you

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.540
The jester's smile

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.420
What's behind the mask?

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:12.260
You can't erase the scars

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.220
No matter how they burn

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:18.050
Let it bloom or let it wither

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:21.020
The setting sun ignites the horizon

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:26.690
Alone in the depths of the night

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:30.860
Let out a cry that can cut through fate

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:33.440
That's the cue to begin

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:37.240
The curtain is rising, it's time to dance

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:41.200
Everybody sheds tears at the end

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:44.080
So hold them in now and keep going

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:48.790
Until the day the curtain falls

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:54.510
The gears will keep turning

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.930
#22 Headed for "Harry"

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.520
A coin toss.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:09.400
You know the game. A coin is tossed.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:15.150
And you choose heads or tails.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.320
So what are the stakes?

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:22.790
Well then, to start with,
I get to touch your body.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.160
What are you thinking, you pervert?

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.460
And if you win,
you want this boy back?

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.080
No, wrong.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:34.050
I get to punch you once.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:40.340
Just one punch? Okay, who's going to toss?

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:43.350
Go ahead, do it.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.570
Which is it?

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:53.610
Heads.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:58.200
It's tails. I win.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:11.040
I'm going to touch you now,
just like we promised.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:12.840
Come here, baby!

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:15.920
No!

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:26.430
How rude. You get to touch this sexy body,
and this is how you do it?

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:30.810
Oh, we're just getting started.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:39.070
Pretty huh? Gotta dress nice and flashy
for a casino.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.530
No way, I'll never wear any of those.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:45.120
Besides, there's no casino here.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:48.450
Then let's bet on making you
get dressed up.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:51.460
And here's the casino.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:58.340
We'll guess where the ball will fall,
in the red or the black.

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:04.970
I get to make you wear whatever I want.
Head, top half, then bottom half.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:09.100
-And you?
-A punch to your face. Red.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:13.100
That again? Okay, here we go.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:28.830
It's black!

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.460
Let's continue.

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:50.100
And lastly, the bottoms.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:53.560
-Red!
-Black.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:04.780
I'm so lucky, it makes me laugh.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.950
You don't have to do it, just run!

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.580
Don't worry.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:13.330
Just don't look while I change.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:19.050
What?

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:22.170
You don't have any luck.

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:26.390
You're not cut out for gambling.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:28.720
I guess not.

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:32.770
Somebody said that to me once before.

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:37.900
I love making fun of people like you
who don't have any luck.

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:42.530
It feels great making them dress
ridiculously and crushing their pride.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:45.780
Those without any luck can't do anything.

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:49.780
But guess what? I survived that war
in the Sahara Desert.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:52.120
And you call that unlucky?

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.830
And what's become of it?

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:56.830
Huh?

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:01.250
You're losing like crazy against me,
and you're about to die.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:07.090
The fact that I was brought into
this battle...

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:12.350
I lost my father and
many other good people.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:19.270
You have a straightforward
and honest punch.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:23.980
You are not good at bargaining
or gambling.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:29.820
If you ever try to gamble
with your life...

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:31.870
you will lose.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:38.460
Maybe this guy is right.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:41.000
Maybe I have no luck.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.880
But I can't run away.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:48.800
On to the next bet. Come with me.

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:03.150
Lord Faceless, the automata
we sent to the US are having trouble.

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:07.240
Hmm, seems like the enemy
is pretty strong.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:10.410
But Blom is over there too.
He can handle it.

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:12.160
Blom, huh.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:16.660
Shall I fly over there too?

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:18.160
Nah, it's fine.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:22.500
Like Graziano says, Blom is already there.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:26.300
But we shouldn't give the humans hope.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:29.340
Just in case.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:32.680
Let's give one of those junk pieces a job.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:39.980
Lady Francine, please allow me to
paint your nails.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:43.980
Would this dress be to your liking?

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:47.610
Perhaps my lady would prefer a bath first?

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:51.700
I've told you again and again.
Leave me alone.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:56.370
I can take care of myself.
Besides, you're my enemies.

00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:00.620
What are you plotting
by pretending to serve me?

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.830
P-Plotting?

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.460
Lady Francine, we just...

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:07.050
Stop it!

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:09.380
I am not Francine.

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:14.680
That's the name of the automaton
you serve. How dare you!

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:18.060
Pantalone.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:21.310
Lord Faceless has a job for you.

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:25.650
Join the troop going to the US
to back up the others.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:32.400
Lady Francine, if you will excuse me.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.830
Going to kill humans again?

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:46.460
I am not Francine, much less your leader.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.710
But hear me.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:54.220
I will never forgive you
if you hurt another human.

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:00.470
We did it somehow.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:03.480
More will come any minute now.
Let's find Harry.

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:08.610
The basement... Damn it.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:21.160
This is where kids with ZONAPHA
lie in agony.

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:25.790
What a wonderful location for our casino.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:28.540
What is this?

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:34.300
Kids with ZONAPHA who couldn't die
become the same as rocks.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:38.720
They don't know how to cure it,
so they have no choice.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:45.140
If Dr. Banhart hadn't invented Harry,
I might've been one of them.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:50.730
Anyway, let's play another game.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:53.280
With the kids as chips.

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:58.120
How about we kill them one at a time
to end their pain?

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:00.410
You lowlife villain!

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:05.870
Thank you.
That's high praise for a gambler.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:08.920
You can't win with that bad luck anyway.

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:15.090
He's right.
I can't win because I have no luck.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:17.680
Don't give up!

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:21.310
I remember what Narumi once said to me.

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:27.690
He said to never give up. To just do
what you can do at any given time.

00:10:29.610 --> 00:10:32.940
Okay, you just shut up now.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:36.950
What I can do...

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:40.700
Jones.

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:43.240
Let's make one last bet.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:46.370
Now we're talking. What's the game?

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:50.330
A coin toss. I say heads.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:52.920
That again?

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:56.130
Okay, fine. I say tails then.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.010
Who's tossing?

00:10:58.180 --> 00:11:01.720
I will this time. And if I win...

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:05.220
I get to punch you once.

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:08.850
That again! Okay, if I win...

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:12.230
I get to kill a kid.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:14.690
Tom.

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:16.690
Thanks.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:36.090
That's dirty...

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.340
You took a hostage. Who's the dirty one?

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:45.100
Besides, you're probably controlling
the coins and wheels with your machines.

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:52.150
Luck was finally with me in the end.

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:53.690
It's heads.

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:56.110
My fluids...

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:59.450
I'm going to boil over...!

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:10.660
Tom, that machine you were talking about.
It cured you of ZONAPHA?

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:13.960
Yeah, I was the first to be tested on.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:19.840
This machine works against
a ZONAPHA bug's working memory.

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:24.970
Once the machine's electromagnetic waves
have driven the bugs from the body,

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:27.970
that person will never be infected again.

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:29.930
Then everyone can be cured?

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:33.060
-Right.
-Does it have a name?

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:34.560
It's Harry.

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:37.820
We named it after this stuffed bear.

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:40.440
That's it, take me there!

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:41.950
Hey!

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:44.950
-Are you okay?
-What took you so long!

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:48.120
I had to deal with one myself.

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:02.670
This ZONAPHA syndrome... It's horrible.

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:06.720
This place is bigger than I thought.

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:09.100
We'll have trouble finding Harry.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:16.860
Ashihana.

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.610
Could you give me one of those?

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:26.240
You made fun of them.
Said they were unhealthy and illogical.

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:30.910
I may have gotten tired of being logical.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:33.250
Well, okay then.

00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:44.510
By the way, I've been meaning to ask you.

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:51.270
I've no idea what you like
about these things.

00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:53.520
So, what is it?

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:58.270
Well, when you came to me again
about this assignment.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:04.490
You're bored.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:07.450
Not again.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:11.950
I listened to you once,
and look what happened in the Sahara.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:14.540
You can't fool me again.

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:18.710
I'm bored.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:26.380
When I was a human, I had a dream,
something I wanted to do.

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:31.810
But there's nothing now that I've become
a shirogane-O.

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:34.730
I can tell.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:38.940
That you don't know what to do
with your life either.

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:45.740
So?

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:50.070
How much are you going to pay me?

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:55.540
What's that dream you were talking about?

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:00.540
I'll tell you when I die.

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:03.300
Anyway, can I borrow these?

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:06.170
I'll give them back
once this fight is over.

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:07.670
Sure.

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:12.010
Oh dear.

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:14.350
Who are you?

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:17.560
It's okay, we're on your side.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:20.230
I'm Ashihana, and he's George.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:25.480
Your face scares them. Do something.

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:27.740
What can I do?

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:33.950
It's okay, don't cry...

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:37.250
Uh oh, what should we do now?

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:41.960
I can play a little.

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:44.670
How about a happy tune?

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:54.100
Let's clap our hands.

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:56.720
Together with the music now.

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.770
Go on, take a bow.

00:16:55.870 --> 00:16:57.280
Um...

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:02.660
George, will you play for us again?

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:09.380
They're here.

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:15.260
Automata, go after the puppeteers.

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:18.510
I'll kill the remaining humans.

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:21.520
Every last one of them.

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:28.360
You must be George Laroche.

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:34.070
You're outdated. You cannot win.
Yet, you will not move?

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:40.660
Sorry George, but I'm outta here.

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:44.210
I can't fight all those things.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:50.960
But I can handle one of them.

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:57.470
It's him...!

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:06.100
I was sent here as a backup
to kill any humans who try to get away.

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:08.190
But there's just one, huh.

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:12.320
You weren't killed in that tent?

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:17.530
Well, you talk as if we've met before.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:23.660
But I do not remember the faces
of the humans I meet.

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:26.040
Of course you don't.

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:29.630
I can't win against him...

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:31.750
But oh well.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.800
I'll let you go. Go on.

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:39.300
Even automata act irregularly at times.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:43.600
Maybe like what humans call "whim."

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:49.440
Humans are going to die out anyway,
so go on.

00:18:55.820 --> 00:19:01.200
You're an old-fashioned machine human
with implanted supplementary mechanisms.

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:08.210
And you're a full robot with a human brain
downloaded into your memory.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:14.210
That's right. I'm most certainly
more advanced than you.

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:17.170
But there you stand, blocking my way.

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:19.090
How curious.

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:24.720
Don't you think it's foolish
to resist me just to die?

00:19:25.520 --> 00:19:26.850
I'm curious, too.

00:19:27.980 --> 00:19:33.150
You became a shirogane because you
suffered from ZONAPHA and wanted revenge.

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:35.610
Why do you now side with the enemy?

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:40.490
Faceless is the person
who created ZONAPHA syndrome.

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:43.120
Bola Misteriosa.

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:46.370
Only rotates 300 times per minute.

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:50.040
Far from my Wunderkugel's
1,000 times per minute.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:52.670
What a fast turning ball that is.

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:56.590
But it's not how fast a CD spins
that matters.

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:00.380
It's the music that it plays.

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:01.930
I couldn't care less.

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:07.930
Lucky me.

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:12.020
No need to look back.

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:16.440
I just have to leave from there.

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:18.780
Move.

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:32.460
Dang it.

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:36.920
I just remembered something so unlike me.

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:41.340
You're bored.

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:45.180
That's right.

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:50.600
I was just like you. Bored with life.

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:55.110
Booze. Women. Gambling.

00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:57.610
All boring.

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:01.900
What's out there for me anyway?

00:21:02.450 --> 00:21:05.490
Only what I've already had too much of.

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:09.330
Time spent in boredom.

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:17.920
There's someone I need to crush
before I can leave here.

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:24.510
The pathetic part of me
that's scared to death by a puppet.

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:31.220
I'm grateful for your offer,
but I'd like to fight.

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:37.360
Well, I was being so generous
but it seems you are a fool.

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:40.150
You may have forgotten.

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:43.820
But you told me to move once.

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:49.950
You, a relative of a household appliance.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:52.790
Talking like that to a human being.

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:57.790
Then come, I will snuff that life out
like a candle for you.

00:21:58.290 --> 00:22:01.050
It's on, Mr. Pantalone.

00:22:27.610 --> 00:22:31.990
Avoiding the crowds, I walk in the dark

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:36.920
And wait with bated breath in the wings

00:22:37.210 --> 00:22:41.630
My expression is calm
while I scream inside

00:22:41.800 --> 00:22:46.590
On the verge of being torn apart

00:22:46.760 --> 00:22:51.390
I dance and beckon you to join me

00:22:51.550 --> 00:22:56.230
As a shadow swings across the stage

00:22:56.390 --> 00:22:59.230
I tell myself this is the last time

00:22:59.400 --> 00:23:05.280
But I can't seem to cut myself free

00:23:05.440 --> 00:23:09.780
Too scared to stop for a moment

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:15.540
My impatience hides
the cries of somebody left behind

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:23.670
Nobody notices the shadow
standing in the sudden rain

00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:31.760
Somewhere far away,
a memory of you is saying goodbye

00:23:31.930 --> 00:23:39.390
I stand here watching,
no longer able to reach you
